> **Mentoring Plan for Muhammad Taky Tahmid**
> 
> As Taky's primary advisor, my mentoring plan for the upcoming year is structured to support his academic growth, professional development, and successful completion of his PhD. The plan focuses on guiding Taky through his dissertation work, facilitating his research dissemination, and preparing him for post-graduate opportunities.
> 
> **1. Research and Dissertation Guidance:**
>    - *Objective*: Successfully complete Taky's dissertation with strong empirical grounding and theoretical contributions.
>    - *Advisor's Role*: I will provide detailed feedback on dissertation chapters, helping refine research questions, analytical methods, and interpretations.
>    - *Mentee's Role*: Taky will deliver draft chapters according to agreed timelines and incorporate feedback to enhance the work.
> 
> **2. Publication and Presentation Strategy:**
>    - *Objective*: Ensure Taky's research reaches a wide audience through reputable journals and conferences.
>    - *Advisor's Role*: Identify suitable journals and conferences, assist in manuscript preparation, and provide feedback on drafts. I will also assist in developing presentation skills through practice sessions and coaching.
>    - *Mentee's Role*: Submit at least one dissertation-related paper to a peer-reviewed journal, present at one national conference, and actively seek feedback to improve presentation skills.
> 
> **3. Career Preparation:**
>    - *Objective*: Prepare Taky for a successful transition into a postdoctoral position, academic role, or policy-oriented job.
>    - *Advisor's Role*: Provide career counseling, help refine his CV and job market materials, and conduct mock interviews. I will also facilitate meetings with professionals in his field of interest.
>    - *Mentee's Role*: Research potential career paths, attend job fairs, and workshops, and apply for relevant positions in alignment with his career goals.
> 
> **4. Professional Development and Networking:**
>    - *Objective*: Broaden Taky’s professional network and expand his exposure to interdisciplinary research.
>    - *Resources*: Encourage participation in seminars, webinars, and workshops offered by the department and other institutions. Provide introductions to colleagues working on similar topics.
>    - *Mentee's Role*: Actively participate in professional development opportunities and seek mentorship from other faculty members and industry professionals.
> 
> **5. Program-Required Mentoring and Support:**
>    - *Objective*: Leverage program resources and fulfill required mentoring activities.
>    - *Program Resources*: Graduate workshops, writing boot camps, and statistical support services available at the university.
>    - *Mentee's Role*: Engage with university resources, regularly review progress with required program milestones, and participate in peer mentoring opportunities where possible.
> 
> By setting specific objectives and clearly defining the roles of both mentor and mentee, this plan aims to ensure that Taky has the support and guidance needed to excel in his academic and professional pursuits. I'm committed to providing the necessary resources and oversight to help him achieve his goals.
> 
